2}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y-x.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-(-2)|=|x+2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)|x+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y(x+2)^{2}-x(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}(x+2)^{2}-xy(x+2)^{2}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(3-2x)(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(-2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+4x+12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{-{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+12x]}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{3}+2+12)-(-8+\\frac{40}{3}+8-24)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((14-\\frac{13}{6})-(-24+\\frac{40}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{135}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02dfae13-8a4c-5f34-8266-509b28f68cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281714} {:answer/id #uuid "953a095e-2b39-500f-a112-434ce1e72136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282976} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c566fe-2323-589c-b6dd-72ddbbda138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5M}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283569} {:answer/id #uuid "f2eec403-255d-543d-9f5a-33b41682ec7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283813} {:answer/id #uuid "f4dc8b91-a62a-5ec4-81ad-834c67ac25d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "953a095e-2b39-500f-a112-434ce1e72136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282976} :answer-field/id #uuid "809bbd0a-3d96-598b-93ab-1eb8237e1da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8d5009c-bf18-5e2c-a10e-cdcea619df0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163621" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 1=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{M}{3}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}({\\int }_{2}^{5}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x-2)^{3}]_{2}^{5}\\cdot {[y]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}(5-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(2-2)^{3})\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(9-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
